  "status": "completed",
  "output": "Now let me verify these trajectories actually replay correctly against the spec — transitions, rewards, and dones:Created `rl_contract/trajectories.jsonl` — 3 trajectories, each verified by replaying against the spec. ✅\n\n**The three trajectories** (states are the pre-action state of each step; `dones[-1]=true` marks the transition into terminal `[2,2]`):\n\n| # | Steps | Path taken |\n|---|---|---|\n| T1 | 4 | Optimal: right, right, down, down |\n| T2 | 5 | Includes an off-grid bump (action `up` at `[0,0]` → stays put, per `off_grid_behavior`) |\n| T3 | 8 | Wanders with a backtrack before reaching the goal |\n\nEach line has `states`, `actions`, `rewards`, `dones` arrays of exactly equal length (4/5/8 respectively).\n\n**Automated checks (all passed):**\n- Every line parses as valid JSON with all four required keys\n- Equal array lengths within each trajectory\n- Every transition matches the deterministic dynamics (including the stay-in-place on the off-grid move)\n- `dones` is `true` exactly when the next state is terminal, and only on the final step\n- All rewards are −1.0, first state of every trajectory is `[0,0]`\n\n**One convention note:** I applied rewards as −1 on *every* step including the terminal-entering one (the classic gridworld reading of \"no additional reward\" in the spec note). If you intended the terminal step to get 0.0 instead, say so and I'll flip those three values.",
